skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Monorepo — plan-credit debit in each store
start
:Reject nonpositive units at C# store boundary;
if (In-memory store?) then (yes)
 :Lock shared gate;
 :Select case-insensitive tenant, active status and current period;
 :Order by configured service credit limit descending;
 :Choose first with sufficient remaining credits;
 :Replace used-credit map; return debit; release lock;
else (PostgreSQL)
 :Call catalog billing.consume_credit;
 :SQL selects exact tenant, active status, period_end > now
and sufficient remaining service credits;
 :Order by configured credit limit descending; LIMIT 1 FOR UPDATE;
 :UPDATE used_credits and updated_at using selected row;
 :Return plan, remaining and period end, or no row;
endif
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Both concrete debit bodies reviewed. PostgreSQL SQL does not check period_start
<= now, unlike the in-memory branch. Both order by credit limit, not remaining headroom
despite the SQL comment. SQL has no own positive-unit guard; the reviewed C# adapter
supplies one. Debit is one database statement, separate from quote approval/consumption
and operation execution. Installed SQL and concurrency acceptance were not tested.
end footer

@enduml
